@@ -8,5 +8,5 @@ export const aComponentIsReadFromItsBodyRatherThanFromItsCallers = {
   claim:
     "`identifier-matches-its-place` reads a component off a function body holding JSX rather than off a caller opening an element with the name. A component holding no JSX, every element for it in another file, is refused under the very name its callers require. `1185e1a2ca` closed the three shapes one file can see. This fourth none can see alone, since the check judges one path at a time. Two findings against instances of it were removed 2026-09-02 as resolved; the instances were, the gap was not.",
   evidence:
-    'Measured 2026-09-02 against the check\'s own `refusedIn`, over every `.ts` and `.tsx` in the repo outside `node_modules`.\n\nThe JSX transform is what makes the capital load-bearing rather than conventional. Through `ts.transpileModule` with `jsx: ReactJSX`, `<Icon x={1} />` emits `_jsx(Icon, { x: 1 })`, the name itself, and `<icon x={1} />` emits `_jsx("icon", { x: 1 })`, a browser tag string. Holding such a name to `lower-camel-case` does not restyle it; it silently makes it a different element.\n\nFour shapes reached `derived-identifier` or `function-identifier` rather than `component-identifier`:\n\n- a name bound to an alias, `const Icon = choice.icon`, then `<Icon />` — 11 places\n- a name bound as a parameter, `({ Icon }) => <Icon />` — 4 places\n- a function holding no JSX that an element in the same file opens with — 4 places\n- a function holding no JSX whose elements are all in other files — the residue\n\n`1185e1a2ca` closed the first three by judging a name an element opens with as a component, looked for as far as that name reaches: the body for a name bound inside one, the file for a declaration. 21 refusals lifted, none inside `akasha/`, none added, 39 tests.\n\nThe residue was `nav-command-bindings-registrar.tsx` line 8, `NavCommandBindings`, gone at `b67a9fd3c7`. The live one is `error-capture-installer.module.code.tsx:16` `ErrorCaptureInstaller`, holding no JSX, its element opened in seven other files.\n\nIt relocated under repair, which is why it is filed rather than absorbed. That registrar was rewritten at `43c1c37a` to return `null` instead of `bindings.map(...)`; removing the inner component pushed the identical refusal up into the parent.\n\nClosing it needs a reading wider than one file, which a change alone cannot give: a caller in an unchanged file is never walked, so one name would be judged differently by what else the change carried.',
+    "Measured 2026-09-02 against the check's own `refusedIn`, over every `.ts` and `.tsx` in the repo outside `node_modules`.\n\nThe JSX transform is what makes the capital load-bearing rather than conventional. Through `ts.transpileModule` with `jsx: ReactJSX`, `<Icon x={1} />` emits `_jsx(Icon, { x: 1 })`, the name itself, and `<icon x={1} />` emits `_jsx(\"icon\", { x: 1 })`, a browser tag string. Holding such a name to `lower-camel-case` does not restyle it; it silently makes it a different element.\n\nFour shapes reached `derived-identifier` or `function-identifier` rather than `component-identifier`:\n\n- a name bound to an alias, `const Icon = choice.icon`, then `<Icon />` — 11 places\n- a name bound as a parameter, `({ Icon }) => <Icon />` — 4 places\n- a function holding no JSX that an element in the same file opens with — 4 places\n- a function holding no JSX whose elements are all in other files — the residue\n\n`1185e1a2ca` closed the first three by judging a name an element opens with as a component, looked for as far as that name reaches: the body for a name bound inside one, the file for a declaration. 21 refusals lifted, none inside `akasha/`, none added, 39 tests.\n\nThe residue was `nav-command-bindings-registrar.tsx` line 8, `NavCommandBindings`, gone at `b67a9fd3c7`. Re-measured 2026-09-06: eleven are live rather than one. `SignUpRoute` in `alan/atlas-web/routes/sign-up.tsx` and again in `alan/web/routes/sign-up.tsx`; `DeepLinkOpenSync`, `DeviceSecretSync`, `NativeAuthRefreshSync`, `DynamicNavCommands`, `OfflineTextSync`, `PushRegistrationSync` and `StatusBarSync` under `alan/web/`; `ErrorCaptureInstaller` at `errors-client/error-capture-installer/error-capture-installer.module.code.tsx:16`; and `PushRegistrationSync` under `smilingjenny/`. Each answers `null` and each is drawn as an element in another file. `StatusBarSync` is the plainest: `alan/web/root.tsx:130` and `alan/web-capacitor/root.tsx:120` both write it as an element, so the lower camel the check demands would compile to an unknown browser tag and the status bar would stop syncing with no error at all.\n\nAll eleven sit in a `.tsx`. Every upper camel function the check refuses in a `.ts` is a genuine miscasing: `Population`, `RemediationDoc`, `TreeSha`, `SymbolId` and the four shape factories in `utils-narrow`. Akasha's own rule is that code drawing for a browser is written in TSX, so the file's ending parts the decidable case from the undecidable one with no caller reading at all.\n\nIt relocated under repair, which is why it is filed rather than absorbed. That registrar was rewritten at `43c1c37a` to return `null` instead of `bindings.map(...)`; removing the inner component pushed the identical refusal up into the parent.\n\nClosing it needs a reading wider than one file, which a change alone cannot give: a caller in an unchanged file is never walked, so one name would be judged differently by what else the change carried.",
 } as const satisfies Finding
